1
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:13,150
Formaldehyde and glutaraldehyde are toxic chemical compounds that are commonly used

2
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:18,270
in laboratories.

3
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:22,750
Exposure to formaldehyde or glutaraldehyde can result in significant adverse effects

4
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:29,750
such as respiratory irritation or impairment, laryngitis, asthma, and bronchitis.

5
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:33,270
Exposure to formaldehyde can also result in cancer.

6
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:38,230
The effects of formaldehyde exposure prompted the Occupational Safety and Health Administration

7
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:45,670
to adopt the formaldehyde standard 29 CFR 1910.1048 to minimize occupational exposure

8
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,010
to formaldehyde.

9
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:52,430
In an ongoing commitment to a consistent culture of safety while working with formaldehyde

10
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:58,310
and glutaraldehyde, follow your laboratory SOPs and OSHA standards.

11
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:03,550
Utilize manufacturer safety data sheets for information on the hazardous characteristics,

12
00:01:03,550 --> 00:01:07,670
exposure routes, and health effects of these chemicals.

13
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:11,630
Follow your laboratory's comprehensive risk management plan.

14
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:15,230
Apply protective measures to prevent exposures.

15
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:19,070
Follow your laboratory's response procedures for incidents.

16
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:22,110
Participate in training and report concerns to your supervisor.
